    "details": "https://github.com/erlang/otp/security/advisories/GHSA-7xgh-gmgf-q2g7\nreports:\n\n> A remote unauthenticated attacker can crash Erlang nodes running the\n> megaco text codec with the flex scanner option by sending an\n> H.248/Megaco message with a property parm name exceeding 452 bytes.\n> The overflow occurs in a C linked-in driver, causing the entire BEAM\n> VM process to terminate. It is reachable pre-authentication, as the\n> flex scanner processes raw TCP payloads before protocol validation.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0352",
